# .env.development is local-dev convenience only - not read by CI or `next build` (see
# .env.production's own comment for why *that* file stays tracked). Its own commented-out
# example shows how to fill in a real Redis keyring secret for local certification against a
# shared dev Redis; tracking it risked that ever being filled in and committed. Defaults are
# documented in .env.example instead.
.env.development

